# MWBM-MEDIA-LANG policy copies (docs/standards/MWBM-MEDIA-LANG.lock).
# They must stay byte for byte identical to the masters in
# MWBMPartners/MeedyaSuite-core — scripts/media-lang/check_copies.py compares
# checksums in CI. Never edit these files here; change the master and run
# check_copies.py --update.
#
# Each line below stops git changing a copy's bytes in four ways: line-ending
# conversion (-text; a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf would otherwise
# fail the check), filters (-filter), encoding conversion
# (-working-tree-encoding) and $Id$ expansion (-ident).
#
# What can still override these lines (git takes each attribute from the
# setting with the highest priority):
#   * any LATER line in this same file that also matches the copy — git uses
#     the last matching line for each attribute, so it need not be a broader
#     one. Keep these lines at the end of the file;
#   * a .gitattributes closer to the copy: in the copy's own folder, or in a
#     folder between the copy and the top of the repository (a deeper file
#     wins over a shallower one). A .gitattributes in a folder that does not
#     contain the copy has no effect on it;
#   * .git/info/attributes on someone's own machine, which git always gives
#     the highest priority.
# The global and system attributes files have the LOWEST priority, so they
# do not override these lines. If anything does change a copy's bytes, the
# copy checker reports that copy as changed.
docs/standards/media-language-bcp47-policy.md -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
docs/standards/MWBM-MEDIA-LANG.lock -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
Tests/Fixtures/MediaLanguage/bcp47-language-policy-v1.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
Tests/Fixtures/MediaLanguage/bcp47-language-policy-v1.schema.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
Sources/MediaLanguagePolicy/Resources/bcp47-language-data-v1.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
Sources/MediaLanguagePolicy/Resources/bcp47-language-data-v1.schema.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
scripts/media-lang/check_copies.py -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
